 "faq_text": "Does Deep Tissue Massage Have to Hurt? No. Deep pressure is never required. Tell me how much pressure you like, and ask me to lighten up at any time; I will. How Is Deep Tissue Massage Different From Therapeutic Massage? Deep tissue massage uses slow, deliberate pressure on muscles that stay tight. Therapeutic massage gives steady attention to the places where you feel tension, at a pace and pressure that suit you. I check in about pressure in both, and each is described on its own page. Can I Choose Where You Focus? Yes. Tell me where you would like me to spend the most time, and you can change it at any point during the session. What Should I Tell You Before a Session? Tell me about any health conditions, medications, pregnancy, recent injury or surgery. I may adjust the work, or suggest you check with your clinician first. New numbness, weakness, unexplained swelling or radiating pain means you should see a doctor before massage. Where Do Sessions Take Place? Sessions take place in Mt. Tabor, Portland. I do not currently travel to clients. How Do I Book a Session? Use the Contact page to reach me by phone or email, and tell me what you would like. I will reply to arrange a time.",
 "image_text": "Illustration of a massage therapist working with a client. Illustration of a therapist massaging a client on a green background. Illustration of a massage therapist working with a client on a bright green background."
